 \subsection{Extensor on Biomimetic Knee}
 
-We tested the extensor configuration on the biomimetic knee with a $\diameter$\qty{10}{\mm} BPA at $l_{0}=\qty{51.8}{\cm}$. The measured torque fell well below both the original prediction and the hybrid calculation (Figure~\ref{fig:Ext10mm_52cm}). Applying the extensor terms identified on the pinned knee improved the prediction: at the adopted two-stage terms, the corrected model reached an RMSE of \qty{1.1702}{\newton\meter}, an FVU of 0.6681, and a maximum absolute residual of \qty{2.2088}{\newton\meter}, against \qty{3.0322}{\newton\meter}, 4.4856, and \qty{5.5870}{\newton\meter} for the original rigid-body prediction. On this configuration the actuator path passes between the femoral condyles close to the instantaneous center of rotation, a geometry that is difficult to represent with the modeled path (Figure~\ref{fig:Ext10mm_52cm}\textbf{A}).
